#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic"&gt;Operation and Maintenance Agreement&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54pt; margin-bottom: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;In July 2017, the Company and an affiliated third party (O&amp;amp;M Provider) entered into an agreement for operation and maintenance of certain transmission facilities. The O&amp;amp;M Provider will operate, maintain, repair and restore the transmission facilities in accordance with the terms and conditions of the agreement, including, without limitation, performing the following: vegetation management, routine maintenance, inspection and assessment services to determine the physical condition of the transmission facilities, outage scheduling, repair and restoration services that become necessary but are not scheduled, other services not otherwise provided for in this agreement as may be proposed by the Company from time-to-time and agreed by the O&amp;amp;M Provider in writing. The O&amp;amp;M Provider is entitled to reimbursement for all operation and maintenance costs reasonably incurred by or on behalf of the Company in accordance with this agreement. The O&amp;amp;M Provider will submit a monthly invoice to the Company within 20 days after the end of each month. On an annual basis, the O&amp;amp;M Provider is required to submit a proposed update to the scheduled maintenance and operations plans and a proposed budget. The Company is required to approve or reject the proposed plan and budget (until an approved plan/budget is fully accepted by both parties). Without approval from the Company, the O&amp;amp;M Provider may not incur operations and maintenance costs that will cause budget overrun unless these costs are in connection with a material adverse event. The agreement sets an initial term of five years from the Project in-service date and thereafter will continue for successive five-year renewal terms unless either party notifies the other in writing at least 180 days prior to the then-current expiration date.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54.35pt; margin-bottom: 7pt; text-indent: -27.35pt; text-align: left; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic"&gt;(b)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 14.52pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic"&gt;Land rights&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54pt; margin-bottom: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company has land rights that were obtained through various easement payments to land owners. These land rights required a one-time upfront payment, are perpetual in nature, and were recorded to Property and equipment, net as incurred.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54.35pt; margin-bottom: 7pt; text-indent: -27.35pt; text-align: left; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic"&gt;(c)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 15.14pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic"&gt;MISO HIMB Project&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54pt; margin-bottom: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;On May 11, 2023, the Company was selected by MISO as the developer of the HIMB Project. The HIMB Project is a 23 mile to 39 mile transmission line in Indiana, depending on the location of the border crossing, with a required in-service date of June 1, 2030. The stated public cost of the project is $77.0 million but the project will exceed this value if the end point location changes and line length increases as is currently anticipated. The Company and MISO expect to refine the project scope mid-2026.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54.35pt; margin-bottom: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company is currently performing development activities, including engineering, routing, permitting, regulatory, and other pre-construction activities. In 2025, the Company entered into service contracts primarily related to engineering and consulting activities, but no material construction agreements have been executed.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54.35pt; margin-bottom: 7pt; text-indent: -27.35pt; text-align: left; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic"&gt;(d)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 14.52pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic"&gt;MISO RIKY Project&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54.35pt; margin-bottom: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;On July 30, 2025, the Company was selected by MISO as the developer of the RIKY Project. The RIKY Project consists of approximately 26 miles of single-circuit 345 kV transmission line connecting the Reid EHV Substation in Kentucky and crossing the Ohio River into Indiana. The project has a required in-service date in 2032, and the expected cost of the project is $85.9 million. &lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54.35pt; margin-bottom: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company is currently performing development activities, including engineering, routing, permitting, regulatory, and other pre-construction activities. In 2025, the Company entered into service contracts primarily related to engineering and consulting activities, but no material construction agreements have been executed.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 27.35pt; margin-bottom: 7pt; text-indent: -27.35pt; text-align: left; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;(6)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 14.52pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Financing Arrangements&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 27pt; margin-bottom: 10pt; page-break-after: avoid"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, outstanding principal balances under the Company's financing arrangements are as follows (in thousands):&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="width: 472.15pt; margin-left: 21.95pt; border-collapse: collapse" class="e-rte-table"&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 20.25pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 1.25pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: left; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 1.2pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: left; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 1.15pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; ve